# Diamond DAG concurrency test: two tasks await the same shared thunk.
# Both tasks should successfully materialize the shared value without cycle errors.
# This tests that spawn_local + settled() correctly handles diamond patterns.
[
  shared: [+ 1 2]
  a: [task [fn [] shared]]
  b: [task [fn [] shared]]
  ra: [await a]
  rb: [await b]
  result: [and [= ra 3] [= rb 3]]
]
=== out
Dict({"shared": Int(3), "a": Task, "b": Task, "ra": Int(3), "rb": Int(3), "result": Variant(Boolean.True, Null)})
